      "unavailable_source_url": null,
      "tweet_url": "https://x.com/CBPAMO/status/1970523860786389398",
      "tweet_type": "original",
      "conversation_id": "1970523860786389398",
      "reply_to_tweet_id": null,
      "reply_to_account": null,
      "reply_to_account_id": null,
      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "🚨SAVING LIVES - On September 18, the Laredo Air Branch responded to a call from U.S. Border Patrol regarding a group in distress in the Petty Ranch area north of Laredo, Texas.\n\nAn AS350 helicopter, with an AMO Agent who is also a certified EMT onboard, quickly located the group and conducted an off-field landing to provide aid. Four individuals, all Mexican nationals, were found in poor condition. One male subject was suffering from a snake bite to his right leg.\n\nThe AMO Agent/EMT stabilized the snake bite victim while coordinating with a medivac helicopter service for transport. The victim was airlifted for further medical care, and the remaining three individuals were transported by U.S. Border Patrol agents for processing.",
      "text_resolved": "🚨SAVING LIVES - On September 18, the Laredo Air Branch responded to a call from U.S. Border Patrol regarding a group in distress in the Petty Ranch area north of Laredo, Texas.\n\nAn AS350 helicopter, with an AMO Agent who is also a certified EMT onboard, quickly located the group and conducted an off-field landing to provide aid. Four individuals, all Mexican nationals, were found in poor condition. One male subject was suffering from a snake bite to his right leg.\n\nThe AMO Agent/EMT stabilized the snake bite victim while coordinating with a medivac helicopter service for transport. The victim was airlifted for further medical care, and the remaining three individuals were transported by U.S. Border Patrol agents for processing.",
